# Python book pipeline (not needed for web app) — EXCEPT scripts/core/
# templates/data/assets-fonts, which api/render-book-html.py needs to render
# a real book_v2 PDF (Create-A-Book). This was the actual root cause of a
# live "ModuleNotFoundError" (2026-08-10): vercel.json's per-function
# includeFiles can only add back files that were actually uploaded — it
# cannot override a repo-wide .vercelignore exclusion, which runs first.
# The "step down, then negate" pattern below is required because
# gitignore-style engines never descend into an already-excluded directory
# to check negations inside it — `!myphonics_books/scripts/x.py` alone would
# silently do nothing while `myphonics_books/` stays excluded. Re-including
# the whole scripts/ directory (rather than naming files one at a time) is
# deliberate — every new local module generate_book.py needs meant another
# round-trip, and scripts/ is only ~18MB, nowhere near Vercel's 500MB cap.
myphonics_books/*
!myphonics_books/scripts
!myphonics_books/core
!myphonics_books/templates
!myphonics_books/assets
!myphonics_books/data

myphonics_books/assets/*
!myphonics_books/assets/fonts

myphonics_apps/

# Marketing assets
marketing/
marketing-mockups/
remotion-transfer/

# Large generated files
output/
*.pdf
*.wav
*.aup3

# Python
__pycache__/
venv/
.venv/
*.pyc

# Generated audio (kept — pre-generated MP3s needed for interactive books)

# Content pipeline
content/
agents/

# Scratch files
public/comparison.html
phonics-explorer.html
MyPhonicsBooks_Visual_Review_unpacked/
